+A negative curvature gives a clipped vertex; nonnegative curvature gives an endpoint maximum.
+When an interval does not determine the sign, the calculation encloses the whole feasible
+portfolio interval. Thus uncertainty enlarges the bound instead of excluding an action. These
+formulas preserve the original continuous control opportunities.
+3.2. Transport across model coefficients
