+4. A SHARP ECONOMIC COMPARISON CONSTRUCTION
+A neural certificate should be compared with independently identified bounds for the same
+economy. We therefore retain the affine-preference market-deflator construction and reimplement
+its numerical evaluation. The lower policy and the upper comparison object are identified
+separately from the neural feedback throughout.
+4.1. Feasible policies and the original stopping contract
+A library policy consists of 16 exact stored consumption constants cj ∈[.7,.8], preference
+actions θj ∈[0,.2], and pj = 0. These controls are held on their time intervals until the original
+first exit. Wealth is deterministic and satisfies
