+transcendental function enters these proof computations. Separate tests compare 807 elementary
+enclosures with 100-digit evaluations; these tests check implementation behavior but do not
+replace the remainder inequalities.
+3.2. Rationally certified Gauss rules
+The eight Gauss–Legendre roots are first proposed by an ordinary floating-point routine. Each
+root is then isolated in a disjoint rational bracket by exact sign evaluations of the degree-eight
+Legendre polynomial and 80 bisections. Eight disjoint sign-changing brackets account for all
+roots. The positive weights are enclosed using
